  "body": "From M3's review of PR #1601 (pullrequestreview-5900553734): `on_ring` (crates/motion/src/ring_zig.rs, about lines 44-69) proves a ramp prefix is on the ring by its **vertices** only, not its **chords**. A D-shaped prefix (a 0.98 rad straight flat whose two end vertices both sit on the circle) still passes and flies as arcs, bulging up to about 0.118 mm past the flat.\n\nOnly the Circular op can reach `push_zig_ring` today, and its prefixes are true ring polygons; that is pinned by the opt-in test `ring_ramps_are_opt_in`. So this is a latent guard gap, not a live gouge.\n\n**Done means:** `on_ring` also requires every prefix chord's sagitta against the ring to be at most `ARC_FIT_TOL`, so a prefix with a long flat falls back to `push_zig` chords. A D-shaped prefix test (flat 0.98 rad) posts chords, mutation-checked (drop the sagitta check, and the test goes red).\n\nRelated: #1558, PR #1601, #1609.\n",
